## Why This Is Asked

Tests mastery of advanced CSS Grid usage, responsive column math, and CSS-only state toggling without JS. It also probes ability to pack variable-height tiles efficiently and to design accessible interactions.

## Key Concepts

- CSS Grid: grid-template-columns, grid-auto-rows: minmax(...), grid-auto-flow: dense

- Responsive design with media queries and CSS variables

- Accessibility: focus-visible, reduced-motion

- CSS-only UI state toggling with data attributes

## Code Example

```css
.grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); grid-gap: var(--gap,16px); grid-auto-rows: minmax(8rem, auto); grid-auto-flow: dense; }
.grid[data-layout="dense"]{ --gap:8px; --pad:8px; }
.card{ padding: var(--pad,12px); aspect-ratio: 16/9; }
.grid > .card:focus-visible{ outline: 2px solid #5b9bd5; transform: translateY(-2px); }
@media (max-width: 1200px){ .grid{ grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 800px){ .grid{ grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){ .grid, .grid > *{ transition: none; } }
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this to 100+ tiles with dynamic content loading while keeping layout stable?
- How would you adapt for dark mode and ensure accessible color contrast?

